"Ludo, explained", a demo film for Tag Team Ludo (JuteBags). English and Hindi voice-over, 16:9 and 9:16.

Picture
- Tag Team Ludo app captures and gameplay recordings (2.5.0 and later): JuteBags' own product.
- Avatars inside the app: Fun Emoji by Davis Uche, CC BY 4.0, generated with DiceBear.
- Fonts: Fredoka and Lilita One (Google Fonts), and Baloo 2 by Ek Type for the Hindi captions (fonts/OFL.txt):
  SIL Open Font License 1.1.

Voice
- Synthetic voice-over. English: Kokoro-82M (hexgrad, Apache 2.0) through kokoro-onnx (MIT), voice "bm_george".
  Hindi: Chatterbox multilingual (Resemble AI, MIT), each line checked and trimmed with faster-whisper (MIT).
  It is a computer voice, not a person.

Sound
- Versilian Community Sample Library (VCSL), github.com/sgossner/VCSL: CC0 1.0 (vibraphone, glockenspiel, hi-hat,
  snare, suspended cymbal).
- Karoryfer Samples, Sneakybass (jazz double bass), github.com/sfzinstruments: CC0 1.0.
- Chiptune voice, kick, dice and foley: synthesized in code.

Made with code-rendered film tools (Lemo-Opuscar library, MIT).
